@@ -15,3 +15,58 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+Sign-up now requests an SMS code, verifies it on the server with Twilio Verify,
+then calls the existing registration service. No account is created by this flow
+until Twilio returns `approved`. Codes and passwords are not stored in browser
+storage or cookies. A signed, HTTP-only cookie binds the phone and username to a
+10-minute verification session, preserves successful verification if registration
+needs a retry, and is cleared after account creation.
+
+Configure the variables in `.env.example` in the Node server's runtime environment
+(the standalone server does not automatically load a project `.env` file).
+`SIGNUP_ORIGIN` must be the exact public origin, including scheme and any port,
+without a trailing slash or path. Use HTTPS in production. Generate a unique
+`SIGNUP_COOKIE_SECRET` with at least 32 random characters and share it across
+instances. Missing configuration disables sign-up with a clear error; there is no
+mock code or verification bypass.
+
+Create a Twilio Verify service with **six-digit codes** and the default **10-minute
+validity**, and configure an approved SMS template. Set its SID in
+`TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID`. Every locale of the template must include a readable
+code and end with the following line, using the actual deployed hostname and
+Twilio's code substitution (the digits here are an example):
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 012345.
+
+@your-deployed-host.example #012345
+```
+
+The final line must contain the hostname only (no scheme, path or port), a single
+space and `#` followed by the generated code, with no signature or trailing text.
+See [Twilio's Verify templates](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api/templates).
+The template is selected explicitly on every SMS request. Keep Verify Fraud Guard,
+geo permissions, send/check attempt limits and deployment-level IP rate limiting
+configured for your traffic. The cookie's 30-second resend delay is a usability
+control; provider and gateway limits must protect against clients clearing cookies.
+
+The single code input supports leading zeros, paste, numeric keyboards and
+`autocomplete="one-time-code"`. WebOTP automatically fills and submits supported
+secure browsers; other browsers retain keyboard suggestions and manual entry.
+WebOTP requests are cancelled on submission, resend, changing details and unmount.
+
+The external registration service remains independently hosted and public. This
+repository can gate its own sign-up route and forwards the verified phone number,
+but cannot enforce verification on direct requests to that external service or
+ensure it persists the phone. Production-wide enforcement requires updating that
+service to require a trusted verification assertion and store the verified number.
+
+Run the isolated server-handler tests without launching a server:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/signup.test.ts
+pnpm build
+```
